  "facts": [
    {
      "id": 1,
      "text": "Some say Gumlog is an amateur translation of the Indian name ‘tsilalu hi’, meaning ‘Sweet‑Gum Settlement,’ while others credit early settlers’ sweet‑gum tree benches for the name.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        26
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gumlog%2C_Georgia",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Gumlog isn’t a sprawling city or a stop on the interstate—it’s a place shaped by its land, its history, and the rhythms of lake life that draw visitors and residents alike.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.eatinoregon.com/what-gumlog-georgia-taught-me-about-small-town-life/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "What I’ve found most striking about Gumlog isn’t just its history or its scenic beauty.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.eatinoregon.com/what-gumlog-georgia-taught-me-about-small-town-life/",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
